Elon Musk is the world's richest man and  he was asked in an interview once would  you rather be a billionaire or a meme  Lord and of course Elon Musk said he'd  rather be a meme Lord now that Meme Lord  activity brought him into the world of  Bitcoin cryptocurrency and he actually  put 1.5 billion dollars of Bitcoin on  the Tesla balance sheet about a year and  a half ago in the summer of last year  they sold 10 of that Bitcoin at a profit  and they said that they were simply  trying to test the market liquidity and  so they had somewhere around 1.2 to 1.3  billion dollars of Bitcoin but in their  most recent Financial disclosures they  went ahead and reported that they sold  75 of their Bitcoin position that's 75  sale netted them about 936 million  dollars onto their balance sheet now you  may remember last July Elon talked about  cryptocurrency and here's what he said I  made pump but I definitely don't dump I  do not believe in getting the price high  and selling or anything like that I  would like to see Bitcoin succeed now  that leads to the question why exactly  is Tesla selling 75 of their Bitcoin  well it's because they needed the cash  elon's quoted as saying that their sale  should not be taken to some verdict on  bitcoin instead Tesla sold his Bitcoin  because it was concerned about overall  liquidity of the company giving covet  shutdowns in China and that they needed  the cash he also states that they did  not sell any of their Dogecoin and he  believes that crypto is a sideshow to  the sideshow now my takeaway from all of  this is that elon's running a business  they need to have a strong balance sheet  they need to have cash flow that's what  he's focused on doing their investment  in Bitcoin he rode the wave he created  plenty of press the critics hated it and  in some way he was sticking it to the  Man by being one of the first public  companies to put Bitcoin on their  balance sheet but the more interesting  takeaway from the recent developments of  this sale is that the market basically  didn't care when they announced that  they had sold 75 percent of their  Bitcoin the market went down like a one  percent or so they literally just did  not care at all that the world's richest  man and one of the largest companies in  the world sold 75 of their Bitcoin  that's because the market is maturing  the impact by one individual or one  company is lessening day by day and  ultimately a more mature Market is  exactly what we should want to see we  don't want to have a market their  response very sensitively to any one  announcement from a business or an  individual instead what you want is a  robust Market structure with deep  liquidity where anyone in the world can  participate and not have to worry about  what's the next press release ready to  drop ultimately Elon Musk he still owns  a ton of Bitcoin SpaceX balance sheet  and personally he also has about 200  million dollars of Bitcoin on the Tesla  balance sheet I think they just needed  the cash and that's okay because in some  ways Bitcoin served as a great store of  value they lost a little bit maybe five  seven eight percent on the Bitcoin  position but if you take into account  inflation in some way Bitcoin actually  held more value over the last 12 months  than cashed it now that's not something  that you'll hear in the mainstream media  hey you did you like this video great we  make five of them a day and post them  here on this channel make sure you  subscribe like the video and see you  next time
 

